---
import AutomaticPocketLayout from "../../layouts/AutomaticPocketLayout.astro";
---

<AutomaticPocketLayout
  title="Automatic Pocket"
  description="Play bass along to real drums and find out, kick by kick, how locked in you are."
>
  <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] italic text-2xl leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)]">
    Play bass along to real drums and find out, kick by kick, how locked in you are.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:gap-8 my-10">
    <figure class="!my-0">
      <img
        src="/images/automatic-pocket/play-portrait.jpg"
        width="640" height="1291"
        alt="The play screen: a needle meter showing the last kick note 18 ms early, the word Locked in, and one bar of a rock groove with a dot where each note landed."
        class="rounded-[1.6rem] shadow-[0_10px_30px_rgba(44,24,16,0.25)]"
      />
      <figcaption>While you play: the needle swings to every kick note, and the bar shows where each one landed.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="!my-0">
      <img
        src="/images/automatic-pocket/results-top.jpg"
        width="640" height="1291"
        alt="The results screen: a pocket score of 68, kicks played, lean and spread, then a row of dots for each kick position in the bar."
        class="rounded-[1.6rem] shadow-[0_10px_30px_rgba(44,24,16,0.25)]"
      />
      <figcaption>After the take: your score, your lean, and each kick in the bar on its own.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Automatic Pocket plays a drum groove in your headphones and listens to your bass through the
    microphone. The rule is simple: play a note on every kick. The score is how tightly those notes
    sit with the kick drum. Everything you play between the kicks is yours, so fills, walk-ups and
    ghost notes never count against you.
  </p>

  <h2>What's in it</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc">
    <li>Ten grooves: rock, funk, soul, disco, hip-hop, half-time, one drop, shuffle, jazz swing and sticks.</li>
    <li>A drummer who can drop out for a few bars while you keep time on your own, or drift the tempo for you to follow.</li>
    <li>Feel targets: push, dead on, laid back, or deep behind the beat.</li>
    <li>Hidden kicks, so you find the kick by ear alone.</li>
    <li>After each take: which kicks in the bar you rush or drag, the notes a listener would hear as off, and every bar at a glance.</li>
    <li>Just drums: put a groove on and play with no scoring, through headphones or the speaker.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you need</h2>
  <p>
    An iPhone or iPad, headphones (wired, USB-C or Bluetooth), and your bass through an amp or played
    unplugged near the device. There's no account, and nothing leaves your device.
  </p>

  <p class="marginalia">Coming soon to the App Store.</p>

  <p>
    Questions or problems: see <a href="/automatic-pocket/support">support</a>. How the app came to be
    is in its <a href="/specimens/automatic-pocket">specimen entry</a>.
  </p>
</AutomaticPocketLayout>
